{"v":1,"dev":"01a077b6-4c36-77bc-879a-5f58767d5cc4","seq":1018,"lc":1018,"ts":1789833253402,"enc":"none","op":"block.set","d":{"pageId":"01a0ba47-8062-73ae-8e5f-d3d4f08eae3c","block":{"absorbedIds":[],"access":null,"content":{"text":""},"createdAt":1789833252677,"frameId":null,"h":null,"id":"01a0ba60-0f45-7052-b289-c1f063083ad8","placement":"snapped","rotation":0.0,"type":"text","updatedAt":1789833252677,"w":200.0,"x":72.0,"y":3408.0,"z":84}}}
{"v":1,"dev":"01a077b6-4c36-77bc-879a-5f58767d5cc4","seq":1019,"lc":1019,"ts":1789833254567,"enc":"none","op":"block.set","d":{"pageId":"01a0ba47-8062-73ae-8e5f-d3d4f08eae3c","block":{"absorbedIds":[],"access":null,"content":{"text":"Here is a concise table covering three common risks, with practical examples, business impact, and mitigations—grounded in standard frameworks like NIST and OWASP.\n\n| Risk | Practical Example | Business Impact | Mitigation 1 | Mitigation 2 |\n|------|-------------------|-----------------|--------------|--------------|\n| **Phishing / Credential Theft** | An employee enters their domain password on a fake login page from a lookalike email. | Account takeover, unauthorized transfers, data breach, regulatory fines, loss of trust. | Enforce phishing-resistant MFA (e.g., FIDO2 security keys) for all users, especially privileged ones. | Run simulated phishing drills with immediate feedback training for those who click. |\n| **Ransomware / Malware** | Malware encrypts a branch file server via a compromised third‑party remote‑access tool. | Service outage, halted transactions, investigation costs, reputational damage. | Maintain offline, immutable backups and test restoration regularly. | Segment the network so endpoint infections can’t reach core banking systems; restrict admin access. |\n| **Unpatched / Vulnerable Systems** | A public‑facing API gateway runs an outdated web server with a known critical CVE, allowing data exfiltration. | Data breach, exposure of customer records, legal liability, PCI‑DSS non‑compliance. | Automate patch management with a defined SLA (e.g., critical patches within 48 hours). | Deploy a WAF and runtime protection to block exploit attempts while patches roll out. |\n\nFor IT operations, the key is consistent monitoring, rapid patching, and assuming breach—so you can detect and respond quickly."},"createdAt":1789833252677,"frameId":null,"h":null,"id":"01a0ba60-0f45-7052-b289-c1f063083ad8","placement":"snapped","rotation":0.0,"type":"text","updatedAt":1789833253849,"w":640.0,"x":72.0,"y":3408.0,"z":84}}}
