{"v":1,"dev":"01a077b6-4c36-77bc-879a-5f58767d5cc4","seq":1212,"lc":1212,"ts":1789833947213,"enc":"none","op":"block.set","d":{"pageId":"01a0ba47-8062-73ae-8e5f-d3d4f08eae3c","block":{"absorbedIds":[],"access":null,"content":{"ink":{"add":[],"base":"c1ef5d1fb3d329361e69be0d6667faaeddda8c8aa45ad2d3524f6bc8f5c3e8fe","gone":"","n":1,"o":[104.50653872282608,5423.4525906656545],"v":1}},"createdAt":1789833946484,"frameId":null,"h":52.33076776597409,"id":"01a0ba6a-a574-7746-a0ea-2afb1cf3542b","placement":"snapped","rotation":0.0,"type":"ink","updatedAt":1789833946484,"w":499.86949573863643,"x":104.50653872282608,"y":5423.4525906656545,"z":147}}}
{"v":1,"dev":"01a077b6-4c36-77bc-879a-5f58767d5cc4","seq":1213,"lc":1213,"ts":1789833972048,"enc":"none","op":"block.set","d":{"pageId":"01a0ba47-8062-73ae-8e5f-d3d4f08eae3c","block":{"absorbedIds":[],"access":null,"content":{"text":""},"createdAt":1789833971308,"frameId":null,"h":null,"id":"01a0ba6b-066c-7047-93c2-101219778f38","placement":"snapped","rotation":0.0,"type":"text","updatedAt":1789833971308,"w":200.0,"x":216.0,"y":5496.0,"z":148}}}
{"v":1,"dev":"01a077b6-4c36-77bc-879a-5f58767d5cc4","seq":1214,"lc":1214,"ts":1789833973174,"enc":"none","op":"block.set","d":{"pageId":"01a0ba47-8062-73ae-8e5f-d3d4f08eae3c","block":{"absorbedIds":[],"access":null,"content":{"text":"Here’s a structured response for the IT operations team.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Initial Investigation Steps\n- **Confirm the issue** – Verify the disruption is real and intermittent (check monitoring alerts, user reports, or reproduce it in a safe test environment).\n- **Check recent changes** – Look for recent deployments, config changes, or infrastructure updates that correlate with the start of the disruptions.\n- **Review logs** – Examine application, API gateway, database, and load balancer logs around the incident timestamps for errors, timeouts, or retries.\n- **Trace a sample transaction** – Follow one failed request end-to-end (client → load balancer → app → DB) to identify where it breaks.\n- **Check dependencies** – Verify upstream/downstream services (payment processor, authentication, messaging queues) are healthy.\n- **Monitor in real time** – Keep dashboards open and watch for patterns (e.g., spikes at certain times, specific endpoints, or user segments).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Infrastructure Metrics to Check\n| Layer | Metrics |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Application** | Error rate, response time (p95/p99), request throughput, thread pool saturation, JVM/GC pauses |\n| **Database** | Connection pool usage, query latency, lock contention, deadlocks, replication lag |\n| **Network** | Packet loss, latency between tiers, DNS resolution time, TLS handshake failures |\n| **Infrastructure** | CPU, memory, disk I/O, network bandwidth on app servers and load balancers |\n| **External dependencies** | Payment gateway response times, third-party API error rates, retry counts |\n| **Load balancer** | Backend health check failures, connection resets, uneven traffic distribution |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Information to Collect Before Escalation\n- **Incident timeline** – When it started, duration, frequency, and whether it’s ongoing.\n- **Affected scope** – Which endpoints, user segments, or regions are impacted; how many requests failed.\n- **Error signatures** – HTTP status codes, exception types, timeout messages, or connection resets.\n- **Log snippets** – Relevant application and infrastructure logs with timestamps.\n- **Metrics screenshots** – Graphs showing the anomaly (e.g., spike in error rate or latency).\n- **Recent change history** – Any deployments, config edits, or scaling events before the incident.\n- **Already attempted** – What checks or non-production actions have been tried, and their results.\n- **Business impact** – Estimated number of affected transactions, customers, or revenue impact (if known).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Short Incident Update for Stakeholders\n\n> **Incident Update – Payment Application Intermittent Disruptions**  \n> **Status:** Investigating  \n> **Start time:** [insert time]  \n> **Impact:** Some customers may experience delays or errors when using the payment application. The issue is intermittent; not all transactions are affected.  \n> **Action:** Our IT operations team is actively investigating. We are reviewing application logs, infrastructure metrics, and recent changes to identify the cause. No production changes have been made without approval.  \n> **Next update:** [insert time or \"within X hours\"]  \n> **Contact:** [on-call lead / incident manager]\n\n---\n\n**Note:** Since the root cause is unknown, avoid speculation in stakeholder updates. Stick to facts, impact, and next steps."},"createdAt":1789833971308,"frameId":null,"h":null,"id":"01a0ba6b-066c-7047-93c2-101219778f38","placement":"snapped","rotation":0.0,"type":"text","updatedAt":1789833972446,"w":640.0,"x":216.0,"y":5496.0,"z":148}}}
{"v":1,"dev":"01a077b6-4c36-77bc-879a-5f58767d5cc4","seq":1215,"lc":1215,"ts":1789833974985,"enc":"none","op":"block.set","d":{"pageId":"01a0ba47-8062-73ae-8e5f-d3d4f08eae3c","block":{"absorbedIds":[],"access":null,"content":{"text":"Here’s a structured response for the IT operations team.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Initial Investigation Steps\n- **Confirm the issue** – Verify the disruption is real and intermittent (check monitoring alerts, user reports, or reproduce it in a safe test environment).\n- **Check recent changes** – Look for recent deployments, config changes, or infrastructure updates that correlate with the start of the disruptions.\n- **Review logs** – Examine application, API gateway, database, and load balancer logs around the incident timestamps for errors, timeouts, or retries.\n- **Trace a sample transaction** – Follow one failed request end-to-end (client → load balancer → app → DB) to identify where it breaks.\n- **Check dependencies** – Verify upstream/downstream services (payment processor, authentication, messaging queues) are healthy.\n- **Monitor in real time** – Keep dashboards open and watch for patterns (e.g., spikes at certain times, specific endpoints, or user segments).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Infrastructure Metrics to Check\n| Layer | Metrics |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Application** | Error rate, response time (p95/p99), request throughput, thread pool saturation, JVM/GC pauses |\n| **Database** | Connection pool usage, query latency, lock contention, deadlocks, replication lag |\n| **Network** | Packet loss, latency between tiers, DNS resolution time, TLS handshake failures |\n| **Infrastructure** | CPU, memory, disk I/O, network bandwidth on app servers and load balancers |\n| **External dependencies** | Payment gateway response times, third-party API error rates, retry counts |\n| **Load balancer** | Backend health check failures, connection resets, uneven traffic distribution |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Information to Collect Before Escalation\n- **Incident timeline** – When it started, duration, frequency, and whether it’s ongoing.\n- **Affected scope** – Which endpoints, user segments, or regions are impacted; how many requests failed.\n- **Error signatures** – HTTP status codes, exception types, timeout messages, or connection resets.\n- **Log snippets** – Relevant application and infrastructure logs with timestamps.\n- **Metrics screenshots** – Graphs showing the anomaly (e.g., spike in error rate or latency).\n- **Recent change history** – Any deployments, config edits, or scaling events before the incident.\n- **Already attempted** – What checks or non-production actions have been tried, and their results.\n- **Business impact** – Estimated number of affected transactions, customers, or revenue impact (if known).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Short Incident Update for Stakeholders\n\n> **Incident Update – Payment Application Intermittent Disruptions**  \n> **Status:** Investigating  \n> **Start time:** [insert time]  \n> **Impact:** Some customers may experience delays or errors when using the payment application. The issue is intermittent; not all transactions are affected.  \n> **Action:** Our IT operations team is actively investigating. We are reviewing application logs, infrastructure metrics, and recent changes to identify the cause. No production changes have been made without approval.  \n> **Next update:** [insert time or \"within X hours\"]  \n> **Contact:** [on-call lead / incident manager]\n\n---\n\n**Note:** Since the root cause is unknown, avoid speculation in stakeholder updates. Stick to facts, impact, and next steps."},"createdAt":1789833971308,"frameId":null,"h":null,"id":"01a0ba6b-066c-7047-93c2-101219778f38","placement":"snapped","rotation":0.0,"type":"text","updatedAt":1789833972446,"w":640.0,"x":144.0,"y":5520.0,"z":148}}}
